---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Install dollarlint" current="/guides/installation/">
  <article class="doc">
    <header class="doc-header">
      <span class="eyebrow">Guide</span>
      <h1>Installation</h1>
      <p class="lead">Install the dollarlint CLI with Go, then point it at any project with JSON, YAML, or TOML config files. It's a small investment that pays dividends.</p>
    </header>

    <h2>Install from source with Go</h2>
    <pre><code>go install github.com/agorischek/dollarlint/cmd/dollarlint@latest</code></pre>
    <p>This installs the <code>dollarlint</code> command from the latest module version available to your Go toolchain.</p>

    <h2>Release binaries</h2>
    <p>The project is configured for GoReleaser and GitHub Releases. Once a release is published, prefer the archive for your platform when you do not want to build from source.</p>

    <h2>Verify the install</h2>
    <pre><code>dollarlint version
dollarlint --help</code></pre>

    <div class="note">
      <p>dollarlint expects a subcommand. Use <code>dollarlint validate .</code>; bare paths such as <code>dollarlint .</code> are intentionally rejected.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</DocsLayout>
